This module was expanded from a prior Julia module by the same author, SSDPClient.jl, which is not in the general registry. The UPnP-specific portions of the module were originally inspired by the Rust UPnP/SSDP ecosystem including crates ssdp and rupnp. Both the ssdp (by Andrew Johnston) and rupnp (by Jakob Hellermann) Rust crates are dual-licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 or the MIT License. 

The current module's Julia implementation has been designed (and later redesigned with names made even less similar to the Rust ecosystem choices) around Julia's standard interfaces and libraries, not the Rust ecosystem. Some code similarities exist, as the libraries are all centered around identical protocols with identical address, port, and similar constraints, and the XML fields used for processing are necessarily identical. The Rust crates have been appreciated but not copied by the process.
